    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0238" n="1072" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1072"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/10412</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-23T20:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1788. For Stewart [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 26. Embassy’s 2122, October 10 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>], 6 p.m.
                    Exceptions outlined are in accordance with those proposed by War Trade Board.
                    Express our gratification at success of these negotiations. Formal conferences
                    now taking place at London, Paris, and Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
